<title>CHINA: Siemens, China firm in ATM deal.</title>
<headline>Siemens, China firm in ATM deal.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Eastern Communications Co Ltd signed a $1.2 million agreement with Siemens AG's Siemens-Nixdorf arm to introduce ATM technology from the German firm, the Xinhua news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>Siemens-Nixdorf would transfer ATM (automated teller machine) production technology to the Chinese company, the agency said without giving further details.</p>
<p>China's central bank has been trying to encourage greater use of ATMs as part of a plan to modernise the nation's banking industry.</p>
</text>
